                  "body": "This allocation change keeps the parameter in FP32, but the default AITER grouped-top-k path still calls `correction_bias_for_dtype(router_logits.dtype)` before routing, so the bias is converted back to BF16 at runtime. Could we preserve FP32 through that fallback and extend `test_glmmoedsa_correction_bias_fp32.py` with a `glm5_next_text` case (including the quantized configs covered here)?",
                  "createdAt": "2026-10-19T15:43:45Z",
                  "databaseId": 4315840233,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -514,7 +514,11 @@ def __init__(\n             correction_bias_dtype = torch.float32\n             # GLM-5.2's bias sits at an offset where its spread is only a few bf16 ULPs\n             # wide, so bf16 collapses it and reorders top-k routing. HF stores it fp32.\n-            if quant_config is not None and not is_glm_moe_dsa(config):\n+            if (\n+                quant_config is not None\n+                and not is_glm_moe_dsa(config)\n+                and getattr(config, \"model_type\", None) != \"glm5_next_text\"",
                  "line": 520,
