    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nOn MI355X with aiter, GLM-5.3-Flash picks MoE experts with a rounded bias. The checkpoint stores each layer's 288 expert correction biases in fp32, within a band about 0.4 wide. With FP8/Quark weights, `MoEGate` casts them to bf16, which steps 0.03–0.06 there; CUDA keeps fp32. 59% of real tokens then change their top-8. This PR keeps the bias fp32 for GLM-5.3-Flash.\r\n\r\nHow the cast swaps an expert, illustrative values:\r\n\r\n| | Expert A | Expert B | Chosen expert (higher val) |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| fp32 bias | 7.410 | 7.420 | |\r\n| Sigmoid score | 0.300 | 0.295 | |\r\n| Score + fp32 bias | 7.710 | **7.715** | B |\r\n| bf16 bias | 7.40625 | 7.40625 | |\r\n| Score + bf16 bias | **7.70625** | 7.70125 | A |\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n\r\nMI355X (gfx95) with aiter. The change keys on `model_type == \"glm5_next_text\"`, so only GLM-5.3-Flash moves; GLM-5.2 already keeps fp32 and other models keep today's dtype. CUDA is untouched.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n| Setting | Value |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| Image | `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.21-rocm10-mi35x-20261012` |\r\n| Base | upstream main `0cf683ea8d` + #41615 + #38764 (GLM-5.3-Flash needs them to run its DSA k-pool on Triton) |\r\n| Model | `amd/GLM-5.3-Flash-Quark-MXFP4`, MI355X TP4 |\r\n| Routing and NLL | prefill only, no MTP; this PR vs this PR with the `glm5_next_text` line removed, so bias dtype is the only difference |\r\n| Text | 1319 GSM8K test problems + 150k tokens of wikitext-103 test (228k tokens) |\r\n\r\nEach layer's 288 checkpoint biases are distinct fp32 values, up to 288 per layer; the bf16 cast leaves at most 11. Replaying real router logits through `biased_grouped_topk_gpu` with each bias, 59% of tokens get a different top-8, mostly by one expert:\r\n\r\n| Experts swapped vs the fp32 bias (42 layers × 18,243 tokens) | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | ≥4 |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| Share of tokens | 41.1% | **43.8%** | 11.8% | 2.5% | 0.7% |\r\n\r\nTeacher-forced NLL over the 228k tokens (mean −log p of each true next token; 95% CI by document bootstrap):\r\n\r\n| Comparison | ΔNLL (nats/token) |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| fp32 bias vs bf16 bias | −0.0014 |\r\n| fp32 bias vs fp32 bias, rerun | −0.0034 | \r\n\r\nA plain rerun moves NLL more than the bf16 cast does, but fp32 is still the correct bias: it is the checkpoint's dtype and what CUDA uses.\r\n\r\n**Accuracy:** GSM8K 97.04 → 96.82 within noise\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38882353575](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38882353575)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38882353490](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38882353490)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38882353542](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38882353542)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
